# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Latar belakang {#background}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The nuclear shell model treats a nucleus as a few *valence* nucleons moving in a small set of\n"
"single-particle orbitals above an inert *core*, interacting through an empirical two-body force\n"
"fitted to measured spectra. It is widely used in low-energy nuclear structure. Its computational cost is\n"
"combinatorial: the basis is every way of distributing the valence protons and neutrons over the\n"
"available states, and this growth limits the model spaces accessible to exact diagonalization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Model kulit (shell model) nuklir memandang inti atom sebagai beberapa nukleon *valensi* yang bergerak dalam sekumpulan kecil\n"
"orbital partikel tunggal di atas *core* yang inert, berinteraksi lewat gaya dua-benda empiris\n"
"yang disesuaikan dengan spektrum terukur. Model ini banyak dipakai dalam struktur nuklir energi rendah. Biaya komputasinya\n"
"kombinatorial: basisnya adalah setiap cara mendistribusikan proton dan neutron valensi ke\n"
"keadaan yang tersedia, dan pertumbuhan ini membatasi ruang model yang bisa dijangkau diagonalisasi eksak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Pooled sample-based quantum diagonalization (pooled SQD) [\\[1\\]](#references) splits that problem in two. A\n"
"quantum circuit is used only to *propose* which basis states matter. It is measured in the\n"
"computational basis, and each measured bitstring names one Slater determinant. The Hamiltonian is\n"
"then built and diagonalized classically in the span of those determinants. Because the classical\n"
"step is an exact diagonalization inside a subspace, it returns a variational upper bound\n"
"on the true ground-state energy, and the bound can only fall as determinants are added.\n"
msgstr ""
"Diagonalisasi kuantum berbasis sampel terkumpul (pooled SQD) [\\[1\\]](#references) membagi masalah itu menjadi dua. Sebuah\n"
"circuit kuantum hanya dipakai untuk *mengusulkan* keadaan basis mana yang penting. Circuit itu diukur dalam\n"
"basis komputasional, dan setiap bitstring hasil pengukuran menamai satu determinan Slater. Hamiltonian\n"
"lalu dibangun dan didiagonalisasi secara klasik dalam span determinan-determinan tersebut. Karena langkah\n"
"klasik ini adalah diagonalisasi eksak di dalam subruang, hasilnya adalah batas atas variasional\n"
"untuk energi keadaan dasar sebenarnya, dan batas itu hanya bisa turun seiring bertambahnya determinan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This division of work makes the method noise-tolerant, with an important limitation. Noise changes *which* determinants the circuit\n"
"proposes. It does not enter the classical Hamiltonian, so it cannot move the eigenvalue of a given\n"
"subspace: a shot that violates a conserved quantity is discarded or repaired, and a shot that\n"
"survives is a legitimate basis vector however it was produced. Noise therefore costs you subspace\n"
"quality, not correctness, and the number you report is an upper bound either way.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pembagian kerja ini membuat metodenya toleran terhadap noise, dengan satu batasan penting. Noise mengubah determinan *mana* yang diusulkan\n"
"circuit. Noise tidak masuk ke Hamiltonian klasik, jadi tidak bisa menggeser nilai eigen dari subruang\n"
"tertentu: shot yang melanggar besaran kekal dibuang atau diperbaiki, dan shot yang\n"
"lolos adalah vektor basis yang sah, bagaimanapun cara menghasilkannya. Jadi noise hanya mengorbankan kualitas\n"
"subruang, bukan kebenaran, dan angka yang Anda laporkan tetap merupakan batas atas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Nuclear structure provides several exact quantum numbers for filtering samples. A physical determinant must carry the right number of valence protons\n"
"*and* the right number of valence neutrons, the right total angular-momentum projection $M_J$, and\n"
"the right parity. Each can be checked with an integer test on a bitstring. The fraction of samples rejected\n"
"depends on the constraint and model space.\n"
msgstr ""
"Struktur nuklir menyediakan beberapa bilangan kuantum eksak untuk menyaring sampel. Determinan fisis harus membawa jumlah proton valensi yang tepat\n"
"*dan* jumlah neutron valensi yang tepat, proyeksi momentum sudut total $M_J$ yang tepat, serta\n"
"paritas yang tepat. Masing-masing bisa dicek dengan uji bilangan bulat pada bitstring. Proporsi sampel yang ditolak\n"
"bergantung pada batasan dan ruang model.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The 24-qubit sd-shell register: three proton orbitals and three neutron orbitals, each split into 2j+1 magnetic substates, one qubit per substate, with the reference determinant of neon-20 filled on the maximal magnetic substates of the 0d5/2 orbital.](/docs/images/tutorials/nuclear-sqd-pooled/sd-shell-register.svg)\n"
msgstr "![The 24-qubit sd-shell register: three proton orbitals and three neutron orbitals, each split into 2j+1 magnetic substates, one qubit per substate, with the reference determinant of neon-20 filled on the maximal magnetic substates of the 0d5/2 orbital.](/docs/images/tutorials/nuclear-sqd-pooled/sd-shell-register.svg)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every qubit is one $m$-scheme single-particle state $(n, \\ell, j, m_j, t_z)$, and $|1\\rangle$ means\n"
"occupied. The register uses a fixed order: protons first, then neutrons; within a species,\n"
"orbitals in file order; within an orbital, $m_j$ descending. The two halves of a bitstring are\n"
"therefore the proton configuration and the neutron configuration. This is the bipartition\n"
"expected by the pooled SQD post-processing tools.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap qubit adalah satu keadaan partikel tunggal skema-$m$ $(n, \\ell, j, m_j, t_z)$, dan $|1\\rangle$ berarti\n"
"terisi. Register memakai urutan tetap: proton dulu, lalu neutron; dalam satu spesies,\n"
"orbital menurut urutan file; dalam satu orbital, $m_j$ menurun. Dua separuh bitstring\n"
"adalah konfigurasi proton dan konfigurasi neutron. Inilah bipartisi\n"
"yang diharapkan oleh alat pasca-pemrosesan pooled SQD.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow {#the-workflow}"
msgstr "Workflow {#the-workflow}"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Workflow diagram: a reference determinant feeds an ensemble of shallow excitation circuits, which are sampled on a QPU to produce bitstrings; the bitstrings are repaired and post-selected on proton and neutron number, recombined into a product subspace where the magnetic projection and parity are imposed, and diagonalized to give a variational upper bound; average occupancies from the resulting eigenvector feed back into the next repair.](/docs/images/tutorials/nuclear-sqd-pooled/sqd-workflow.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Workflow diagram: a reference determinant feeds an ensemble of shallow excitation circuits, which are sampled on a QPU to produce bitstrings; the bitstrings are repaired and post-selected on proton and neutron number, recombined into a product subspace where the magnetic projection and parity are imposed, and diagonalized to give a variational upper bound; average occupancies from the resulting eigenvector feed back into the next repair.](/docs/images/tutorials/nuclear-sqd-pooled/sqd-workflow.svg)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two stages in the diagram handle the nuclear symmetries.\n"
msgstr "Dua tahap dalam diagram menangani simetri nuklir.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Repair and post-selection** handle samples affected by hardware noise. The two half-register nucleon numbers\n"
"are Hamming weights, so `qiskit-addon-sqd` handles them directly: `recover_configurations` repairs a\n"
"broken bitstring by flipping the bits least consistent with the current estimate of the average\n"
"orbital occupancies, rather than throwing the shot away.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Perbaikan dan pasca-seleksi** menangani sampel yang terpengaruh noise perangkat keras. Dua jumlah nukleon separuh-register\n"
"adalah bobot Hamming, jadi `qiskit-addon-sqd` menanganinya secara langsung: `recover_configurations` memperbaiki\n"
"bitstring yang rusak dengan membalik bit yang paling tidak konsisten dengan estimasi terkini dari rata-rata\n"
"okupansi orbital, alih-alih membuang shot tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The product subspace** introduces $M_J$. Because $M_J = M_p + M_n$ couples the two halves, it\n"
"is not a property of either one, so it must not be used to filter whole shots: a bitstring whose\n"
"proton half and neutron half are each valid still contributes two good half-configurations even when\n"
"its total $M_J$ is wrong. The subspace is therefore spanned by every *product* of a sampled proton\n"
"configuration with a sampled neutron configuration, keeping the products that land in the target\n"
"$M_J$ and parity sector. This is the pooled SQD subspace construction, and it means a few thousand\n"
"bitstrings can span a subspace far larger than the sample count.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Subruang produk** memperkenalkan $M_J$. Karena $M_J = M_p + M_n$ mengaitkan kedua separuh, ia\n"
"bukan properti salah satunya, jadi tidak boleh dipakai untuk menyaring seluruh shot: bitstring yang separuh\n"
"proton dan separuh neutronnya masing-masing valid tetap menyumbang dua setengah-konfigurasi yang baik meskipun\n"
"$M_J$ totalnya salah. Jadi subruang direntang oleh setiap *produk* dari konfigurasi proton\n"
"yang disampel dengan konfigurasi neutron yang disampel, dengan mempertahankan produk yang jatuh di sektor\n"
"$M_J$ dan paritas target. Inilah konstruksi subruang pooled SQD, dan artinya beberapa ribu\n"
"bitstring bisa merentang subruang yang jauh lebih besar daripada jumlah sampel.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two governing equations {#two-governing-equations}"
msgstr "Dua persamaan utama {#two-governing-equations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The shell-model Hamiltonian is a one-body term plus a two-body interaction,\n"
msgstr "Hamiltonian shell-model adalah suku satu-benda ditambah interaksi dua-benda,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation}\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"H = \\sum_{p} \\varepsilon_p\\, a_p^\\dagger a_p\n"
"  + \\tfrac{1}{4}\\sum_{pqrs} \\langle pq \\| rs \\rangle\\, a_p^\\dagger a_q^\\dagger a_s a_r ,\n"
"\\end{equation}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation}\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"H = \\sum_{p} \\varepsilon_p\\, a_p^\\dagger a_p\n"
"  + \\tfrac{1}{4}\\sum_{pqrs} \\langle pq \\| rs \\rangle\\, a_p^\\dagger a_q^\\dagger a_s a_r ,\n"
"\\end{equation}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $p,q,r,s$ label $m$-scheme states and $t_z = -1$ for a proton, $+1$ for a neutron. Empirical\n"
"interactions such as USDA [\\[2\\]](#references) and GXPF1 [\\[3\\]](#references) are tabulated not in\n"
"the $m$-scheme but in the $J$-coupled basis, as matrix elements $\\langle ab; J | V | cd; J \\rangle$\n"
"between normalized antisymmetrized two-body states of *orbitals* $a,b,c,d$. Recovering the\n"
"$m$-scheme element is a Clebsch-Gordan recoupling,\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana $p,q,r,s$ melabeli keadaan skema-$m$ dan $t_z = -1$ untuk proton, $+1$ untuk neutron. Interaksi\n"
"empiris seperti USDA [\\[2\\]](#references) dan GXPF1 [\\[3\\]](#references) ditabulasikan bukan dalam\n"
"skema-$m$ melainkan dalam basis berpasangan-$J$, sebagai elemen matriks $\\langle ab; J | V | cd; J \\rangle$\n"
"antara keadaan dua-benda ternormalisasi dan teranti-simetrisasi dari *orbital* $a,b,c,d$. Memulihkan\n"
"elemen skema-$m$ adalah rekopling Clebsch-Gordan,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation}\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"\\langle pq \\| rs \\rangle = \\sqrt{1 + \\delta_{ab}}\\sqrt{1 + \\delta_{cd}}\n"
"  \\sum_{J} \\langle j_p m_p\\, j_q m_q | J M \\rangle\n"
"           \\langle j_r m_r\\, j_s m_s | J M \\rangle\n"
"           \\langle ab; J | V | cd; J \\rangle ,\n"
"\\end{equation}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation}\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"\\langle pq \\| rs \\rangle = \\sqrt{1 + \\delta_{ab}}\\sqrt{1 + \\delta_{cd}}\n"
"  \\sum_{J} \\langle j_p m_p\\, j_q m_q | J M \\rangle\n"
"           \\langle j_r m_r\\, j_s m_s | J M \\rangle\n"
"           \\langle ab; J | V | cd; J \\rangle ,\n"
"\\end{equation}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"with the $\\sqrt{1+\\delta}$ factors undoing the normalization convention of the tabulated states.\n"
"Everything else in this tutorial is built on these two equations.\n"
msgstr ""
"dengan faktor $\\sqrt{1+\\delta}$ yang membatalkan konvensi normalisasi dari keadaan yang ditabulasikan.\n"
"Semua hal lain dalam tutorial ini dibangun di atas dua persamaan ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The three runs {#the-three-runs}"
msgstr "Tiga eksekusi {#the-three-runs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | Nucleus | Shell | Qubits | Symmetry-allowed basis | Exactly checkable? |\n"
"|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n"
"| Small-scale | $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ (2p + 2n) | $sd$ | 24 | 640 | Yes |\n"
"| Large-scale | $^{44}\\mathrm{Ti}$ (2p + 2n) | $pf$ | 40 | 4,000 | Yes |\n"
"| Large-scale | $^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$ (4p + 4n) | $pf$ | 40 | 1,963,461 | No |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | Nukleus | Kulit | Qubit | Basis yang diizinkan simetri | Bisa dicek secara eksak? |\n"
"|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n"
"| Skala kecil | $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ (2p + 2n) | $sd$ | 24 | 640 | Ya |\n"
"| Skala besar | $^{44}\\mathrm{Ti}$ (2p + 2n) | $pf$ | 40 | 4,000 | Ya |\n"
"| Skala besar | $^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$ (4p + 4n) | $pf$ | 40 | 1,963,461 | Tidak |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The small-scale run is the walkthrough. Both large-scale runs use a 40-qubit register: the first is\n"
"still small enough to diagonalize exactly on a laptop, so you can compare the hardware result with an exact reference. The second exceeds the\n"
"exact-diagonalization capacity of this tutorial.\n"
msgstr ""
"Eksekusi skala kecil adalah panduan langkah demi langkah. Kedua eksekusi skala besar memakai register 40-qubit: yang pertama\n"
"masih cukup kecil untuk didiagonalisasi secara eksak di laptop, jadi Anda bisa membandingkan hasil perangkat keras dengan referensi eksak. Yang kedua melampaui\n"
"kapasitas diagonalisasi eksak tutorial ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Every run here executes on a QPU.** That is a choice made for this tutorial rather than a\n"
"requirement of the method: all three runs share a backend and a gate budget so you can compare their performance\n"
"at different problem sizes.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Setiap eksekusi di sini berjalan di QPU.** Itu pilihan untuk tutorial ini, bukan\n"
"syarat dari metodenya: ketiga eksekusi memakai backend dan anggaran gate yang sama supaya Anda bisa membandingkan performanya\n"
"pada ukuran masalah yang berbeda.\n"

