# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You also need an IBM Quantum&reg; account with credentials saved locally, and access to a QPU\n"
"with at least 40 qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Anda juga butuh akun IBM Quantum&reg; dengan kredensial yang tersimpan secara lokal, serta akses ke QPU\n"
"dengan minimal 40 qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"No simulator package is needed, and no data files have to be downloaded. The two interaction files\n"
"this tutorial uses are embedded in the following setup cell and written to a temporary directory when you\n"
"run it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tidak perlu paket simulator, dan tidak ada file data yang harus diunduh. Dua file interaksi\n"
"yang dipakai tutorial ini sudah tertanam di sel penyiapan berikut dan ditulis ke direktori sementara saat Anda\n"
"menjalankannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Penyiapan {#setup}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This section imports the tools and defines the shell-model helpers the workflow needs, in the order\n"
"the workflow uses them. The physics behind each one is derived in the [Appendix](#appendix); the\n"
"comments describe each function’s role in the workflow.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bagian ini mengimpor alat dan mendefinisikan helper shell-model yang dibutuhkan workflow, sesuai urutan\n"
"yang dipakai workflow. Fisika di balik masing-masing diturunkan di [Lampiran](#appendix); komentar\n"
"menjelaskan peran tiap fungsi dalam workflow.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Two interaction files are unpacked first. Both are published parameter sets, embedded here so the\n"
"notebook is self-contained: `usda.snt` is the USDA $sd$-shell Hamiltonian [\\[2\\]](#references) and\n"
"`gxpf1.snt` is the GXPF1 $pf$-shell Hamiltonian [\\[3\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr ""
"Dua file interaksi diekstrak lebih dulu. Keduanya adalah set parameter yang dipublikasikan, ditanamkan di sini agar\n"
"notebook mandiri: `usda.snt` adalah Hamiltonian kulit-$sd$ USDA [\\[2\\]](#references) dan\n"
"`gxpf1.snt` adalah Hamiltonian kulit-$pf$ GXPF1 [\\[3\\]](#references).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The model space and the qubit register {#the-model-space-and-the-qubit-register}"
msgstr "Ruang model dan register qubit {#the-model-space-and-the-qubit-register}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An `.snt` file holds the model space, the single-particle energies, and the $J$-coupled two-body\n"
"matrix elements. For the mass-dependent interactions used here, the third and fourth fields of the two-body\n"
"header specify the reference mass\n"
"$A_{\\mathrm{ref}}$ at which the interaction was fitted and the exponent of its mass dependence. Both\n"
"files carry the exponent $-0.3$, with $A_{\\mathrm{ref}} = 18$ for USDA and $42$ for GXPF1, so the\n"
"tabulated matrix elements must be rescaled by $(A/A_{\\mathrm{ref}})^{-0.3}$ for the nucleus being\n"
"computed [\\[2\\]](#references), [\\[3\\]](#references). Single-particle energies are not rescaled. Skipping\n"
"this step changes the correlation energy by a few percent.\n"
msgstr ""
"File `.snt` berisi ruang model, energi partikel tunggal, dan elemen matriks dua-benda berpasangan-$J$.\n"
"Untuk interaksi yang bergantung pada massa yang dipakai di sini, field ketiga dan keempat dari header dua-benda\n"
"menentukan massa referensi\n"
"$A_{\\mathrm{ref}}$ tempat interaksi disesuaikan dan eksponen dari ketergantungan massanya. Kedua\n"
"file membawa eksponen $-0.3$, dengan $A_{\\mathrm{ref}} = 18$ untuk USDA dan $42$ untuk GXPF1, jadi\n"
"elemen matriks yang ditabulasikan harus diskalakan ulang dengan $(A/A_{\\mathrm{ref}})^{-0.3}$ untuk nukleus yang\n"
"dihitung [\\[2\\]](#references), [\\[3\\]](#references). Energi partikel tunggal tidak diskalakan ulang. Melewati\n"
"langkah ini mengubah energi korelasi beberapa persen.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The energies that follow are *valence* energies, measured from the inert core; they are not experimental\n"
"separation energies.\n"
msgstr ""
"Energi berikut adalah energi *valensi*, diukur dari core yang inert; bukan energi\n"
"pemisahan eksperimental.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Clebsch-Gordan recoupling {#clebsch-gordan-recoupling}"
msgstr "Rekopling Clebsch-Gordan {#clebsch-gordan-recoupling}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Equation (2) requires Clebsch-Gordan coefficients for half-integer angular momenta. Every argument is\n"
"passed as *twice* its physical value, so $j = 5/2$ enters as `5` and the arithmetic stays exact.\n"
msgstr ""
"Persamaan (2) membutuhkan koefisien Clebsch-Gordan untuk momentum sudut setengah-bilangan bulat. Setiap argumen\n"
"diberikan sebagai *dua kali* nilai fisisnya, jadi $j = 5/2$ masuk sebagai `5` dan aritmetikanya tetap eksak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`Interaction.v_ms` handles lookups of the interaction matrix elements. An `.snt` file stores each\n"
"matrix element once, so a lookup might need the antisymmetrized pair-exchange phase $-(-1)^{j_a + j_b - J}$ on either\n"
"side, and the bra and ket might be stored in either order.\n"
msgstr ""
"`Interaction.v_ms` menangani pencarian elemen matriks interaksi. File `.snt` menyimpan setiap\n"
"elemen matriks sekali saja, jadi pencarian mungkin butuh fase pertukaran-pasangan teranti-simetrisasi $-(-1)^{j_a + j_b - J}$ di salah satu\n"
"sisi, dan bra serta ket mungkin tersimpan dalam urutan apa pun.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Matrix elements and the symmetry test {#matrix-elements-and-the-symmetry-test}"
msgstr "Elemen matriks dan uji simetri {#matrix-elements-and-the-symmetry-test}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A determinant is a sorted tuple of occupied qubit indices. Two determinants differing in more than\n"
"two occupied states have a vanishing matrix element; otherwise, the Slater-Condon rules give a short\n"
"sum over the interaction, multiplied by a fermionic sign counting how many occupied states lie between the\n"
"operators in the fixed register ordering.\n"
msgstr ""
"Determinan adalah tuple terurut dari indeks qubit yang terisi. Dua determinan yang berbeda lebih dari\n"
"dua keadaan terisi punya elemen matriks nol; selain itu, aturan Slater-Condon memberikan\n"
"jumlah pendek atas interaksi, dikalikan tanda fermionik yang menghitung berapa banyak keadaan terisi berada di antara\n"
"operator dalam urutan register tetap.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`symmetry_allowed` is the integer test that all four exact quantum numbers reduce to. It is used both\n"
"to filter samples and to enumerate the exact basis for the runs small enough to check.\n"
msgstr ""
"`symmetry_allowed` adalah uji bilangan bulat yang menjadi tujuan reduksi keempat bilangan kuantum eksak. Fungsi ini dipakai baik untuk\n"
"menyaring sampel maupun untuk mengenumerasi basis eksak pada eksekusi yang cukup kecil untuk dicek.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The reference determinant {#the-reference-determinant}"
msgstr "Determinan referensi {#the-reference-determinant}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The ansatz is built on top of a single determinant, so that determinant should be the best one\n"
"available. Filling the lowest single-particle energies ignores the two-body interaction. In these model\n"
"spaces, that choice gives an energy 1–2 MeV above the lowest-energy determinant.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ansatz dibangun di atas satu determinan, jadi determinan itu harus yang terbaik\n"
"yang tersedia. Mengisi energi partikel tunggal terendah mengabaikan interaksi dua-benda. Dalam ruang model\n"
"ini, pilihan itu memberi energi 1–2 MeV di atas determinan berenergi terendah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Restricting to fillings made of time-reversed $(+m_j, -m_j)$ pairs forces $M_J = 0$ exactly and\n"
"leaves only $\\binom{n_{\\mathrm{pairs}}}{k}$ candidates per species (a few thousand at most), so the\n"
"best one can be found by searching them all on the full diagonal $\\langle \\Phi | H | \\Phi \\rangle$.\n"
"Ties go to the most strongly aligned pairs, where the $J = 0$ pairing force is strongest. In every\n"
"case in this tutorial that can be checked against a full enumeration, the search returns the global\n"
"lowest-diagonal determinant, which is also the largest single component of the exact ground state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Membatasi pada pengisian yang terdiri dari pasangan berbalik-waktu $(+m_j, -m_j)$ memaksa $M_J = 0$ secara eksak dan\n"
"hanya menyisakan $\\binom{n_{\\mathrm{pairs}}}{k}$ kandidat per spesies (paling banyak beberapa ribu), sehingga\n"
"yang terbaik bisa ditemukan dengan mencari semuanya pada diagonal penuh $\\langle \\Phi | H | \\Phi \\rangle$.\n"
"Jika seri, dipilih pasangan yang paling selaras, tempat gaya pairing $J = 0$ paling kuat. Dalam setiap\n"
"kasus di tutorial ini yang bisa dicek terhadap enumerasi penuh, pencarian mengembalikan determinan dengan\n"
"diagonal terendah global, yang juga merupakan komponen tunggal terbesar dari keadaan dasar eksak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The excitation pool and its perturbative ranking {#the-excitation-pool-and-its-perturbative-ranking}"
msgstr "Pool eksitasi dan peringkat perturbatifnya {#the-excitation-pool-and-its-perturbative-ranking}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Correlation is carried by two-particle–two-hole ($2p2h$) excitations from the reference. Two\n"
"selection rules reduce the pool before any circuit is built: an excitation must conserve $M_J$, and the hole pair and particle\n"
"pair must be able to couple to a common total $J$, which is a triangle inequality.\n"
msgstr ""
"Korelasi dibawa oleh eksitasi dua-partikel–dua-lubang ($2p2h$) dari referensi. Dua\n"
"aturan seleksi memangkas pool sebelum circuit apa pun dibangun: eksitasi harus mengonservasi $M_J$, dan pasangan lubang serta pasangan\n"
"partikel harus bisa berpasangan ke $J$ total yang sama, yaitu ketaksamaan segitiga.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The remaining excitations are ranked by the Epstein-Nesbet second-order score of selected configuration interaction\n"
"[\\[4\\]](#references),\n"
msgstr ""
"Eksitasi yang tersisa diberi peringkat dengan skor orde kedua Epstein-Nesbet dari interaksi konfigurasi terpilih\n"
"[\\[4\\]](#references),\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation}\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"s_\\alpha = \\frac{|\\langle \\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}} | H | \\alpha \\rangle|^2}{|\\Delta_\\alpha|},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\Delta_\\alpha = H_{\\mathrm{ref},\\mathrm{ref}} - H_{\\alpha\\alpha},\n"
"\\end{equation}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation}\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"s_\\alpha = \\frac{|\\langle \\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}} | H | \\alpha \\rangle|^2}{|\\Delta_\\alpha|},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\Delta_\\alpha = H_{\\mathrm{ref},\\mathrm{ref}} - H_{\\alpha\\alpha},\n"
"\\end{equation}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"which estimates how much correlation energy each excitation carries. The same two numbers fix the\n"
"circuit angle: with $V = \\langle \\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}} | H | \\alpha \\rangle$, the first-order amplitude\n"
"is $t_\\alpha = V / \\Delta_\\alpha$. The [Appendix](#appendix) explains why the first-order amplitude is\n"
"the choice used in this tutorial rather than the exact two-level angle.\n"
msgstr ""
"yang memperkirakan seberapa besar energi korelasi yang dibawa tiap eksitasi. Dua bilangan yang sama menentukan\n"
"sudut circuit: dengan $V = \\langle \\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}} | H | \\alpha \\rangle$, amplitudo orde pertama\n"
"adalah $t_\\alpha = V / \\Delta_\\alpha$. [Lampiran](#appendix) menjelaskan mengapa amplitudo orde pertama menjadi\n"
"pilihan di tutorial ini dan bukan sudut dua-level yang eksak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qubit-excitation blocks {#qubit-excitation-blocks}"
msgstr "Blok eksitasi qubit {#qubit-excitation-blocks}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Under the Jordan-Wigner mapping a particle-conserving $2p2h$ excitation operator becomes a sum of\n"
"eight Pauli strings, each carrying a string of $Z$ operators between the outermost indices. The\n"
"$Z$ strings enforce fermionic antisymmetry, and they are expensive: a proton-neutron\n"
"excitation spans the boundary between the two halves of the register and includes a parity string\n"
"across that boundary.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di bawah pemetaan Jordan-Wigner, operator eksitasi $2p2h$ yang mengonservasi partikel menjadi jumlah\n"
"delapan string Pauli, masing-masing membawa string operator $Z$ di antara indeks terluar. String\n"
"$Z$ menegakkan antisimetri fermionik, dan mahal: eksitasi proton-neutron\n"
"melintasi batas antara dua separuh register dan menyertakan string paritas\n"
"di seberang batas itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Dropping the $Z$ strings gives the *qubit-excitation* operator of Yordanov et al.\n"
"[\\[5\\]](#references). The state prepared by this operator has different amplitudes, but it connects exactly the same pairs of determinants, so the set of determinants the circuit can\n"
"reach is unchanged. Pooled SQD uses these determinants for the classical diagonalization. Step 2 compares\n"
"the support of the two constructions and measures their hardware costs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Membuang string $Z$ menghasilkan operator *eksitasi qubit* dari Yordanov dkk.\n"
"[\\[5\\]](#references). Keadaan yang disiapkan operator ini punya amplitudo berbeda, tetapi menghubungkan pasangan determinan yang persis sama, jadi himpunan determinan yang bisa\n"
"dijangkau circuit tidak berubah. Pooled SQD memakai determinan ini untuk diagonalisasi klasik. Langkah 2 membandingkan\n"
"dukungan kedua konstruksi dan mengukur biaya perangkat kerasnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Building the Pauli form from $a_j^\\dagger = \\tfrac{1}{2}(X_j - i Y_j) \\otimes Z_{<j}$, with the $Z$\n"
"string optional, keeps the two constructions a single flag apart. All eight terms of one generator\n"
"commute, so a single `PauliEvolutionGate` step is the exact exponential rather than a Trotter\n"
"approximation to it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Membangun bentuk Pauli dari $a_j^\\dagger = \\tfrac{1}{2}(X_j - i Y_j) \\otimes Z_{<j}$, dengan string $Z$\n"
"opsional, membuat kedua konstruksi hanya berbeda satu flag. Kedelapan suku dari satu generator\n"
"komutatif, jadi satu langkah `PauliEvolutionGate` adalah eksponensial eksak, bukan pendekatan\n"
"Trotter darinya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The depth budget and the circuit ensemble {#the-depth-budget-and-the-circuit-ensemble}"
msgstr "Anggaran kedalaman dan ensemble circuit {#the-depth-budget-and-the-circuit-ensemble}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A single deep circuit containing every ranked excitation can exceed the hardware’s coherence time. Spreading the pool\n"
"over an *ensemble* of shallow circuits and pooling their shots into one determinant set turns Step 2\n"
"into a packing problem: each excitation has a measured cost, each circuit has a budget, and the\n"
"question is how much of the ranked pool fits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Satu circuit dalam yang memuat setiap eksitasi berperingkat bisa melebihi waktu koherensi perangkat keras. Menyebar pool\n"
"ke *ensemble* circuit dangkal dan menggabungkan shot-nya menjadi satu himpunan determinan mengubah Langkah 2\n"
"menjadi masalah pengepakan: tiap eksitasi punya biaya terukur, tiap circuit punya anggaran, dan\n"
"pertanyaannya adalah berapa banyak pool berperingkat yang muat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The budget is measured in **two-qubit depth** (layers of two-qubit gates on the critical path)\n"
"rather than in a raw gate count, because depth sets the circuit's duration and therefore how\n"
"much of the device's coherence it spends. The total count is reported alongside it, since that is the\n"
"better proxy for accumulated gate error; the two answer different questions and neither substitutes\n"
"for the other.\n"
msgstr ""
"Anggaran diukur dalam **kedalaman dua-qubit** (lapisan gate dua-qubit pada jalur kritis)\n"
"bukan jumlah gate mentah, karena kedalaman menentukan durasi circuit dan dengan demikian seberapa\n"
"banyak koherensi perangkat yang terpakai. Jumlah totalnya dilaporkan bersamanya, karena itu\n"
"proksi yang lebih baik untuk akumulasi error gate; keduanya menjawab pertanyaan berbeda dan tidak saling\n"
"menggantikan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Both quantities are extracted by *arity*: an instruction acting on exactly two qubits, whatever the\n"
"backend happens to call its entangling gate. Matching on gate names instead could return zero\n"
"for an unfamiliar basis set, incorrectly placing the whole pool in one circuit without exceeding\n"
"the computed budget.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kedua besaran diekstrak berdasarkan *arity*: instruksi yang bekerja pada tepat dua qubit, apa pun yang\n"
"disebut backend sebagai gate entangling-nya. Mencocokkan nama gate bisa mengembalikan nol\n"
"untuk set basis yang tidak dikenal, sehingga keliru menaruh seluruh pool di satu circuit tanpa melebihi\n"
"anggaran yang dihitung.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Filling whichever circuit is currently emptiest, in rank order, keeps every circuit near the budget.\n"
"Costs are measured on the real backend target, one excitation at a time, because a cost read off an\n"
"abstract circuit is not the cost the transpiler produces.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mengisi circuit mana pun yang saat ini paling kosong, menurut urutan peringkat, menjaga setiap circuit mendekati anggaran.\n"
"Biaya diukur pada target backend sungguhan, satu eksitasi sekali waktu, karena biaya yang dibaca dari circuit\n"
"abstrak bukanlah biaya yang dihasilkan transpiler.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Post-processing: repair, recombine, diagonalize {#post-processing-repair-recombine-diagonalize}"
msgstr "Pasca-pemrosesan: perbaiki, gabungkan ulang, diagonalisasi {#post-processing-repair-recombine-diagonalize}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Three helpers do the work of Step 4.\n"
msgstr "Tiga helper mengerjakan Langkah 4.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`half_configurations` splits each sampled row into a proton half and a neutron half, and keeps each\n"
"half that has the correct nucleon number. A row with a valid proton half contributes that half even if its\n"
"neutron half has the wrong nucleon number. Each half carries the total sampled weight of the rows it appeared in, which\n"
"is what ranks it if the subspace needs to be truncated.\n"
msgstr ""
"`half_configurations` memecah setiap baris sampel menjadi separuh proton dan separuh neutron, dan mempertahankan setiap\n"
"separuh yang punya jumlah nukleon benar. Baris dengan separuh proton valid tetap menyumbang separuh itu meskipun\n"
"separuh neutronnya punya jumlah nukleon yang salah. Setiap separuh membawa total bobot sampel dari baris tempat ia muncul, yang\n"
"menjadi dasar peringkatnya jika subruang perlu dipangkas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`grow_subspace` recombines the halves into every product that lands in the target $M_J$ and parity\n"
"sector, *adding* to the subspace it is given rather than rebuilding it. That keeps successive\n"
"subspaces nested, which is what makes the energy sequence monotone non-increasing instead of merely\n"
"fluctuating around a bound.\n"
msgstr ""
"`grow_subspace` menggabungkan ulang separuh-separuh itu menjadi setiap produk yang jatuh di sektor $M_J$ dan paritas\n"
"target, *menambahkan* ke subruang yang diberikan alih-alih membangunnya ulang. Itu menjaga subruang\n"
"berurutan tetap bersarang, yang membuat deret energi monoton tak-naik dan bukan sekadar\n"
"berfluktuasi di sekitar sebuah batas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`recovery_loop` is the self-consistent configuration recovery of the pooled SQD paper\n"
"[\\[1\\]](#references): repair the two half-register nucleon numbers against the current occupancy\n"
"estimate, recombine, diagonalize, and take the next occupancy estimate from the eigenvector.\n"
msgstr ""
"`recovery_loop` adalah pemulihan konfigurasi self-consistent dari makalah pooled SQD\n"
"[\\[1\\]](#references): perbaiki dua jumlah nukleon separuh-register terhadap estimasi okupansi\n"
"terkini, gabungkan ulang, diagonalisasi, dan ambil estimasi okupansi berikutnya dari vektor eigen.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Check the bit-ordering conventions carefully to avoid incorrect results. `qiskit-addon-sqd` writes column 0 of its\n"
"bitstring matrix as the *highest* qubit index, so reversing a row gives occupation indexed by qubit;\n"
"its \"right\" half is the low qubit indices, which is the proton block. Correspondingly,\n"
"`recover_configurations` takes `num_elec_a` as the proton number and average occupancies ordered\n"
"`(protons, neutrons)` by qubit index. The addon assumes bit $i$ pairs with bit $i + N$; in this\n"
"register, proton qubit $i$ and neutron qubit $i + N$ are the same $(n, \\ell, j, m_j)$ state, so the\n"
"assumption is physically meaningful here rather than incidental.\n"
msgstr ""
"Periksa konvensi urutan bit dengan cermat agar tidak ada hasil yang salah. `qiskit-addon-sqd` menulis kolom 0 dari\n"
"matriks bitstring-nya sebagai indeks qubit *tertinggi*, jadi membalik baris memberi okupansi yang diindeks menurut qubit;\n"
"separuh \"kanan\"-nya adalah indeks qubit rendah, yaitu blok proton. Sejalan dengan itu,\n"
"`recover_configurations` menerima `num_elec_a` sebagai jumlah proton dan okupansi rata-rata yang berurutan\n"
"`(protons, neutrons)` menurut indeks qubit. Addon mengasumsikan bit $i$ berpasangan dengan bit $i + N$; dalam\n"
"register ini, qubit proton $i$ dan qubit neutron $i + N$ adalah keadaan $(n, \\ell, j, m_j)$ yang sama, jadi\n"
"asumsi itu bermakna secara fisis di sini, bukan kebetulan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Backend, budget, and run parameters {#backend-budget-and-run-parameters}"
msgstr "Backend, anggaran, dan parameter eksekusi {#backend-budget-and-run-parameters}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every run that follows uses the same backend, the same pass managers, and the same depth budget, so the three\n"
"are directly comparable. The budget ties them together: every circuit in every\n"
"ensemble has to fit inside it, and it decides how much of a pool can be sampled at all.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap eksekusi berikut memakai backend yang sama, pass manager yang sama, dan anggaran kedalaman yang sama, jadi ketiganya\n"
"bisa dibandingkan langsung. Anggaran itu mengikat ketiganya: setiap circuit di setiap\n"
"ensemble harus muat di dalamnya, dan anggaran menentukan seberapa banyak pool yang bisa disampel.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The values here were chosen by measuring transpiled cost against a Heron target. At a two-qubit depth of 300 and 16 circuits, both 24-qubit and 40-qubit ensembles come out well under 100 microseconds per\n"
"circuit, against coherence times of a few hundred microseconds. Increasing the budget includes more of the pool but increases circuit duration. Measure this\n"
"tradeoff for your backend.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nilai di sini dipilih dengan mengukur biaya hasil transpilasi terhadap target Heron. Pada kedalaman dua-qubit 300 dan 16 circuit, ensemble 24-qubit maupun 40-qubit berada jauh di bawah 100 mikrodetik per\n"
"circuit, dibandingkan waktu koherensi beberapa ratus mikrodetik. Menaikkan anggaran memasukkan lebih banyak pool tetapi menambah durasi circuit. Ukur\n"
"tradeoff ini untuk backend Anda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale hardware example {#small-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Contoh perangkat keras skala kecil {#small-scale-hardware-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This section follows the four-step workflow on a QPU, using the same backend and the same\n"
"gate budget as the large-scale runs. The smaller problem provides an exact reference for checking the result.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bagian ini mengikuti workflow empat langkah pada QPU, dengan backend yang sama dan anggaran\n"
"gate yang sama seperti eksekusi skala besar. Masalah yang lebih kecil menyediakan referensi eksak untuk mengecek hasilnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The small-scale problem is $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$: two valence protons and two valence neutrons in the\n"
"$sd$ shell above an $^{16}\\mathrm{O}$ core, with the USDA interaction [\\[2\\]](#references). Three\n"
"orbitals per species give 24 qubits, and the complete symmetry-allowed basis is 640 determinants,\n"
"small enough to compare the energy estimates with the exact answer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Masalah skala kecilnya adalah $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$: dua proton valensi dan dua neutron valensi di\n"
"kulit $sd$ di atas core $^{16}\\mathrm{O}$, dengan interaksi USDA [\\[2\\]](#references). Tiga\n"
"orbital per spesies memberi 24 qubit, dan basis lengkap yang diizinkan simetri adalah 640 determinan,\n"
"cukup kecil untuk membandingkan estimasi energi dengan jawaban eksak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Petakan input klasik ke masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Read the interaction, build the register, and construct the reference determinant. The following table shows the register information from the [Background](#background), read directly\n"
"from the interaction file.\n"
msgstr ""
"Baca interaksi, bangun register, dan susun determinan referensi. Tabel berikut menunjukkan informasi register dari [Latar belakang](#background), dibaca langsung\n"
"dari file interaksi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Run two checks on the Hamiltonian before continuing. Both are inexpensive and can reveal\n"
"recoupling errors that a single energy calculation might not detect.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jalankan dua pengecekan pada Hamiltonian sebelum melanjutkan. Keduanya murah dan bisa mengungkap\n"
"kesalahan rekopling yang mungkin tidak terdeteksi oleh satu perhitungan energi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A rotationally invariant Hamiltonian organizes its eigenstates into $J$ multiplets, so every\n"
"eigenvalue of the $M_J = 2$ sector must also appear in the $M_J = 0$ spectrum at the same energy. The gap between the ground state and the lowest state carrying $M_J = 2$ is the $2^+$ excitation\n"
"energy, which is measured: $1.634$ MeV for $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ [\\[6\\]](#references). An empirical\n"
"$sd$-shell interaction is expected to agree within a few hundred keV.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hamiltonian yang invarian secara rotasi mengatur keadaan eigennya menjadi multiplet $J$, jadi setiap\n"
"nilai eigen sektor $M_J = 2$ juga harus muncul di spektrum $M_J = 0$ pada energi yang sama. Selisih antara keadaan dasar dan keadaan terendah yang membawa $M_J = 2$ adalah energi\n"
"eksitasi $2^+$, yang terukur: $1.634$ MeV untuk $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ [\\[6\\]](#references). Interaksi\n"
"kulit-$sd$ empiris diharapkan cocok dalam beberapa ratus keV.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, construct the operator pool. Applying the two selection rules gives an important result: for this reference, in this model space, **there are no allowed single excitations at all**.\n"
msgstr "Selanjutnya, susun pool operator. Menerapkan dua aturan seleksi memberi hasil penting: untuk referensi ini, di ruang model ini, **sama sekali tidak ada eksitasi tunggal yang diizinkan**.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The reason is specific and checkable. A $1p1h$ excitation conserves $M_J$ only if the particle state\n"
"has the same $m_j$ as the hole. The reference occupies the two states of largest $|m_j|$ in the\n"
"lowest orbital ($m_j = \\pm 5/2$ of $0d_{5/2}$), and no other orbital in the $sd$ shell reaches\n"
"$|m_j| = 5/2$, since $0d_{3/2}$ stops at $3/2$ and $1s_{1/2}$ at $1/2$. Therefore, no single excitation\n"
"survives, and correlation is carried entirely by $2p2h$ excitations. This is a property of the\n"
"reference and the shell, not a general law; the following cell counts it rather than assuming it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alasannya spesifik dan bisa dicek. Eksitasi $1p1h$ mengonservasi $M_J$ hanya jika keadaan partikel\n"
"punya $m_j$ yang sama dengan lubang. Referensi menempati dua keadaan dengan $|m_j|$ terbesar di\n"
"orbital terendah ($m_j = \\pm 5/2$ dari $0d_{5/2}$), dan tidak ada orbital lain di kulit $sd$ yang mencapai\n"
"$|m_j| = 5/2$, karena $0d_{3/2}$ berhenti di $3/2$ dan $1s_{1/2}$ di $1/2$. Jadi, tidak ada eksitasi tunggal\n"
"yang bertahan, dan korelasi sepenuhnya dibawa oleh eksitasi $2p2h$. Ini adalah properti dari\n"
"referensi dan kulit, bukan hukum umum; sel berikut menghitungnya dan tidak mengasumsikannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Optimalkan masalah untuk eksekusi pada perangkat keras kuantum {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Transpilation reveals the hardware cost of the Jordan-Wigner $Z$ strings and the savings from\n"
"using qubit excitations. The first cell measures both constructions against the real backend\n"
"target and checks the claim, introduced in the [Setup](#setup), that dropping the $Z$ strings changes the\n"
"amplitudes but not the set of determinants the circuit can reach.\n"
msgstr ""
"Transpilasi memperlihatkan biaya perangkat keras dari string $Z$ Jordan-Wigner dan penghematan dari\n"
"memakai eksitasi qubit. Sel pertama mengukur kedua konstruksi terhadap target backend\n"
"sungguhan dan mengecek klaim, yang diperkenalkan di [Penyiapan](#setup), bahwa membuang string $Z$ mengubah\n"
"amplitudo tetapi tidak mengubah himpunan determinan yang bisa dijangkau circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compare two consequences of this substitution. A qubit excitation costs the same regardless of the distance between its\n"
"indices, so proton-neutron excitations, which span the boundary between the two halves of the\n"
"register and make up most of the pool, no longer have this additional cost. The whole pool then\n"
"fits inside the budget, which means the limit on the result is sampling rather than circuit depth.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bandingkan dua konsekuensi dari substitusi ini. Eksitasi qubit berbiaya sama berapa pun jarak antara\n"
"indeksnya, jadi eksitasi proton-neutron, yang melintasi batas antara dua separuh\n"
"register dan membentuk sebagian besar pool, tidak lagi menanggung biaya tambahan ini. Seluruh pool kemudian\n"
"muat dalam anggaran, artinya batas pada hasil adalah sampling, bukan kedalaman circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Eksekusi menggunakan primitive Qiskit {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Submit one job per problem, with the whole ensemble as a single list of circuits. Gate and\n"
"measurement twirling and dynamical decoupling are enabled to reduce the effects of hardware noise.\n"
"Their benefit depends on the circuit and backend.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kirim satu job per masalah, dengan seluruh ensemble sebagai satu daftar circuit. Twirling gate dan\n"
"pengukuran serta dynamical decoupling diaktifkan untuk mengurangi efek noise perangkat keras.\n"
"Manfaatnya bergantung pada circuit dan backend.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each job’s ID is printed. Use `service.job(\"JOB_ID\")` to retrieve the completed job and its\n"
"results without using additional QPU time.\n"
msgstr ""
"ID setiap job dicetak. Gunakan `service.job(\"JOB_ID\")` untuk mengambil job yang sudah selesai beserta\n"
"hasilnya tanpa memakai waktu QPU tambahan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Pasca-proses dan kembalikan hasil dalam format klasik yang diinginkan {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Convert the quantum samples into an energy estimate using the nuclear-symmetry constraints\n"
"described in the [Background](#background) section.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ubah sampel kuantum menjadi estimasi energi menggunakan batasan simetri nuklir\n"
"yang dijelaskan di bagian [Latar belakang](#background).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Configuration recovery repairs the two nucleon numbers.** `recover_configurations` takes each shot that\n"
"has the wrong number of protons or neutrons and flips the bits least consistent with the current\n"
"estimate of the average orbital occupancies, instead of discarding it. On the first pass the\n"
"occupancy estimate comes from the shots that already survived; afterward it comes from the\n"
"eigenvector of the previous subspace, which makes the procedure self-consistent.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pemulihan konfigurasi memperbaiki dua jumlah nukleon.** `recover_configurations` mengambil setiap shot yang\n"
"punya jumlah proton atau neutron yang salah dan membalik bit yang paling tidak konsisten dengan estimasi\n"
"terkini dari rata-rata okupansi orbital, alih-alih membuangnya. Pada putaran pertama\n"
"estimasi okupansi berasal dari shot yang sudah lolos; setelah itu berasal dari\n"
"vektor eigen subruang sebelumnya, yang membuat prosedurnya self-consistent.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**$M_J$ and parity are imposed on the recombined products, not on whole shots.** Every repaired shot\n"
"contributes a proton half and a neutron half, and the subspace is spanned by every product of a\n"
"sampled proton configuration with a sampled neutron configuration that lands at $M_J = 0$ with the\n"
"right parity. Filtering whole shots on total $M_J$ instead would throw away two good halves for the\n"
"sake of a quantum number that belongs to their combination.\n"
msgstr ""
"**$M_J$ dan paritas diberlakukan pada produk hasil gabungan ulang, bukan pada seluruh shot.** Setiap shot yang diperbaiki\n"
"menyumbang separuh proton dan separuh neutron, dan subruang direntang oleh setiap produk dari\n"
"konfigurasi proton yang disampel dengan konfigurasi neutron yang disampel yang jatuh pada $M_J = 0$ dengan\n"
"paritas yang benar. Menyaring seluruh shot berdasarkan $M_J$ total justru akan membuang dua separuh yang baik demi\n"
"sebuah bilangan kuantum yang melekat pada kombinasinya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The four quantum-number checks reject different fractions of samples. The two nucleon numbers\n"
"account for most of the filtering. Parity is *automatically* satisfied inside a single major shell: every $sd$ orbital\n"
"has even $\\ell$ and every $pf$ orbital odd $\\ell$, so once the nucleon numbers are right the parity\n"
"cannot be wrong. The parity check is retained because a cross-shell model space would make it an\n"
"independent constraint. The $M_J$ check keeps products in the target angular-momentum sector. The value of\n"
"having four exact quantum numbers is that they are *cheap and exact*, not that each one is a large\n"
"filter.\n"
msgstr ""
"Empat pengecekan bilangan kuantum menolak proporsi sampel yang berbeda. Dua jumlah nukleon\n"
"menyumbang sebagian besar penyaringan. Paritas terpenuhi *secara otomatis* di dalam satu kulit utama: setiap orbital $sd$\n"
"berlangsung $\\ell$ genap dan setiap orbital $pf$ $\\ell$ ganjil, jadi begitu jumlah nukleon benar, paritas\n"
"tidak mungkin salah. Pengecekan paritas tetap dipertahankan karena ruang model lintas-kulit akan menjadikannya\n"
"batasan yang independen. Pengecekan $M_J$ mempertahankan produk di sektor momentum sudut target. Nilai dari\n"
"memiliki empat bilangan kuantum eksak adalah bahwa semuanya *murah dan eksak*, bukan bahwa masing-masing adalah filter\n"
"besar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Diagonalizing gives a variational upper bound.** Because each iteration's subspace contains the\n"
"last, the sequence of energies falls monotonically, and every entry in it is a rigorous upper bound on\n"
"the true ground-state energy, regardless of the noise in the samples that produced it.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Diagonalisasi memberikan batas atas variasional.** Karena subruang setiap iterasi memuat\n"
"subruang sebelumnya, deret energi turun secara monoton, dan setiap entri di dalamnya adalah batas atas yang ketat untuk\n"
"energi keadaan dasar sebenarnya, terlepas dari noise pada sampel yang menghasilkannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Evaluate the results {#evaluate-the-results}"
msgstr "Evaluasi hasilnya {#evaluate-the-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the following checks to evaluate your results on a Heron-class backend with these settings:\n"
msgstr "Gunakan pengecekan berikut untuk mengevaluasi hasil Anda pada backend kelas Heron dengan pengaturan ini:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Shot survival** on the two nucleon numbers measures the fraction of shots with the correct proton and neutron counts. It can fall as\n"
"the register grows. A survival rate near zero can indicate a problem with circuit execution. Check the ISA depth in Step 2 and the backend's calibration, not the post-processing.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kelangsungan shot** pada dua jumlah nukleon mengukur proporsi shot dengan jumlah proton dan neutron yang benar. Proporsi ini bisa turun seiring\n"
"register membesar. Tingkat kelangsungan mendekati nol bisa menandakan masalah pada eksekusi circuit. Periksa kedalaman ISA di Langkah 2 dan kalibrasi backend, bukan pasca-pemrosesan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The recovery loop** should print a subspace dimension that stays constant or grows and an energy that stays constant or falls with\n"
"each iteration. If iteration 1 already reaches `MAX_DIMENSION`, the classical solver rather than the\n"
"sampling is the binding constraint.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Loop pemulihan** seharusnya mencetak dimensi subruang yang tetap atau bertambah dan energi yang tetap atau turun pada\n"
"setiap iterasi. Jika iterasi 1 sudah mencapai `MAX_DIMENSION`, maka solver klasik, bukan\n"
"sampling, yang menjadi kendala pengikat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The recovered fraction** for $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ should be high, because the ansatz ceiling\n"
"computed in Step 1 is the full 640-determinant space; this run is where sampling, not\n"
"expressiveness, is the only obstacle.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Fraksi yang dipulihkan** untuk $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ seharusnya tinggi, karena batas atas ansatz\n"
"yang dihitung di Langkah 1 adalah seluruh ruang 640 determinan; pada eksekusi ini sampling, bukan\n"
"ekspresivitas, satu-satunya hambatan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The two assertions** in the preceding cell check the variational bounds. A bound that rises means the\n"
"subspaces stopped being nested, and a bound below the exact energy means something is wrong with the\n"
"Hamiltonian, not with the hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Dua assertion** di sel sebelumnya mengecek batas variasional. Batas yang naik berarti\n"
"subruang berhenti bersarang, dan batas di bawah energi eksak berarti ada yang salah pada\n"
"Hamiltonian, bukan pada perangkat keras.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Counterintuitively, a *noisier* backend can give a slightly better bound than a clean one, because\n"
"errors produce valid half-configurations the ideal circuit would never have sampled, and widening\n"
"a variational subspace cannot raise its lowest eigenvalue. Noisy simulation can demonstrate the same effect; this tutorial shows it with\n"
"hardware samples.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara kontraintuitif, backend yang *lebih berisik* bisa memberi batas yang sedikit lebih baik daripada yang bersih, karena\n"
"error menghasilkan setengah-konfigurasi valid yang tidak akan pernah disampel circuit ideal, dan memperluas\n"
"subruang variasional tidak bisa menaikkan nilai eigen terendahnya. Simulasi berisik bisa memperlihatkan efek yang sama; tutorial ini menunjukkannya dengan\n"
"sampel perangkat keras.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/nuclear-sqd-pooled/extracted-outputs/c040-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/nuclear-sqd-pooled/extracted-outputs/c040-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Contoh perangkat keras skala besar {#large-scale-hardware-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Scaling up changes only the inputs, so the next step is to combine the four stages into one function\n"
"and run it twice, both times on a 40-qubit register in the $pf$ shell above a\n"
"$^{40}\\mathrm{Ca}$ core with the GXPF1 interaction [\\[3\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr ""
"Meningkatkan skala hanya mengubah input, jadi langkah berikutnya adalah menggabungkan keempat tahap menjadi satu fungsi\n"
"dan menjalankannya dua kali, keduanya pada register 40-qubit di kulit $pf$ di atas\n"
"core $^{40}\\mathrm{Ca}$ dengan interaksi GXPF1 [\\[3\\]](#references).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two runs illustrate different aspects of scaling:\n"
msgstr "Kedua eksekusi menggambarkan aspek peningkatan skala yang berbeda:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$^{44}\\mathrm{Ti}$, two valence protons and two valence neutrons, has a 4,000-determinant basis. The\n"
"register is 40 qubits, but the problem is still small enough to diagonalize exactly on a laptop, so\n"
"you can compare the hardware result with an exact reference after increasing the register size.\n"
msgstr ""
"$^{44}\\mathrm{Ti}$, dua proton valensi dan dua neutron valensi, punya basis 4,000 determinan. \n"
"Registernya 40 qubit, tetapi masalahnya masih cukup kecil untuk didiagonalisasi secara eksak di laptop, jadi\n"
"Anda bisa membandingkan hasil perangkat keras dengan referensi eksak setelah memperbesar ukuran register.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$, four valence protons and four valence neutrons, has 1,963,461 symmetry-allowed determinants in the same 40 qubits.\n"
"The tutorial's dense solver cannot diagonalize that full space, so the run returns\n"
"a rigorous upper bound and the reference determinant it improves on.\n"
msgstr ""
"$^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$, empat proton valensi dan empat neutron valensi, punya 1,963,461 determinan yang diizinkan simetri dalam 40 qubit yang sama.\n"
"Solver padat tutorial ini tidak bisa mendiagonalisasi seluruh ruang itu, jadi eksekusinya mengembalikan\n"
"batas atas yang ketat dan determinan referensi yang diperbaikinya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Watch two quantities across the two runs. The fraction of the pool that fits inside the fixed gate\n"
"budget shrinks as the pool grows, and `pack_ensemble` reports how much is included. The\n"
"subspace stops being limited by sampling and starts being limited by `MAX_DIMENSION`, the largest\n"
"matrix the dense classical solver here builds. At this scale, a production\n"
"calculation would use a selected configuration interaction (selected-CI) solver.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan dua besaran pada kedua eksekusi. Proporsi pool yang muat dalam anggaran\n"
"gate tetap mengecil seiring pool membesar, dan `pack_ensemble` melaporkan berapa banyak yang disertakan. \n"
"Subruang berhenti dibatasi oleh sampling dan mulai dibatasi oleh `MAX_DIMENSION`, matriks\n"
"terbesar yang dibangun solver klasik padat di sini. Pada skala ini, perhitungan\n"
"produksi akan memakai solver selected configuration interaction (selected-CI).\n"

